5. DEFLATIONARY MECHANISMS & MARKET STABILIZATION
To mitigate token devaluation and encourage long-term holding behavior (HODL), the ecosystem incorporates multiple on-chain deflationary and stabilization mechanisms.
Native Burn Functionality (ERC20Burnable)
The PNJC.sol contract permanently includes a standardized burn() function.
Unused allocations from:
•	Marketing pools;
•	Airdrop reserves;
•	Special community deflationary events;
may be irreversibly destroyed on-chain, permanently reducing circulating supply.
Volatility Isolation via Vesting
The implementation of PNJC_Vesting.sol with cliff-based lockups prevents large token volumes from entering circulation simultaneously.
Decentralized Treasury Management
Reserve pools are maintained within advanced multi-signature wallet structures, preventing impulsive market actions by individual team members.
