8. INSTITUTIONAL SECURITY GOVERNANCE FRAMEWORK
The ecosystem’s reserve funds, including Treasury and Charity pools, are protected through a multi-layered institutional-grade security architecture.
1. Multi-Signature Safe Architecture
Any asset movement outside automated staking contracts requires approval from at least 5 out of 7 independently verified signatory keys distributed among trusted Web3 ecosystem participants.
Unilateral unauthorized access is technically impossible.
2. Hardware Security Isolation
All private keys associated with ecosystem governance are generated and stored using isolated enterprise-grade Hardware Security Modules (HSMs) and Ledger/Trezor Enterprise hardware wallets, minimizing risks associated with phishing or remote compromise.
3. Quota & Tranche-Based Allocation System
Marketing and infrastructure development budgets are strictly limited through tranche-based release mechanisms tied directly to roadmap milestones.
This structure protects the ecosystem against premature reserve depletion.
